WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.480
Did that one TVA agent's voice sound creepily&nbsp;
familiar on the second season premiere of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.080
"Loki"? If it did, you're probably a "Call&nbsp;
of Duty" fan. Here's how you may know him.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.560
Minor spoilers for Loki Season 2 Episode 1 ahead!

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.640
Most everyone knows that Marvel's Disney+&nbsp;
original series "Loki" stars Tom Hiddleston&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:20.200
as the title's trickster god of Norse&nbsp;
mythology, complete with shiny hair and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.800
an irrepressible need to be the snarkiest&nbsp;
person in the room. Plenty of members of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.320
the supporting cast are quite well known as&nbsp;
well, such as Owen Wilson and Gugu Mbatha-Raw,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.120
or the most recent addition to the&nbsp;
ensemble, Oscar winner Ke Huy Quan.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:37.200
But not everyone in the cast is an award winner or&nbsp;
a top-billed star, at least not yet. For example:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.320
Neil Ellice, a Scottish actor whose&nbsp;
voice might be more famous than his face.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.400
On "Loki," Ellice portrays Hunter D-90,&nbsp;
the stick-in-the-mud Minuteman who prunes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:50.440
Wilson's Mobius on the orders of Mbatha-Raw's&nbsp;
Ravonna Renslayer. He changes his tune after he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:53.840
realizes that every single member of the&nbsp;
Time Variance Authority is a kidnapped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:58.760
memory-wiped, and brainwashed variant, stolen from&nbsp;
somewhere on the timeline. Apparently, it's a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:03.400
harder to commit genocide when you qualify as a&nbsp;
potential candidate for the murder spree yourself.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:07.080
Like many supporting cast members, Ellice&nbsp;
returns for "Loki" Season 2 and has a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.160
delightfully awkward conversation&nbsp;
with Mobius in which he almost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:14.480
but not quite, apologizes for&nbsp;
the whole "killing him" thing.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:18.920
"Mobius, I was just doing my job."
"You mean, pruning me? Yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.000
well. I guess you were just following orders."

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.560
Ellice seems to find great success in his&nbsp;
portrayals of soldiers who know how to follow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:29.120
orders. Obviously, there's Hunter D-90,&nbsp;
but there's also Captain John MacTavish,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.680
better known by his code name, Soap, from the&nbsp;
"Call of Duty" video game franchise. Ellice voices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.680
the character in multiple "Modern Warfare"&nbsp;
entries and numerous spinoff games. Outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.600
of these projects, however, which he proudly&nbsp;
features at the top of his social media pages,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:46.600
his résumé is relatively sparse, with his only&nbsp;
other roles unnamed background characters.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:50.240
Before entering the professional screen and&nbsp;
voice acting business, Ellice performed on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.360
stage. His education prepared him for live&nbsp;
theater; he trained at the National Youth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.880
Theatre of Great Britain and the Royal Academy&nbsp;
of Dramatic Art's Shakespeare Summer School. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.840
that means that our muscle-bound Minuteman is&nbsp;
a former theater kid. He's also something of an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:07.040
outdoorsman, based on his love of hiking and the&nbsp;
countryside. On top of all that, he appears to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:12.480
be a dedicated gym bro. This is starting to sound&nbsp;
dangerously like a dating profile bio, isn't it?

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.240
In November 2022, Ellice sat down with Dan Allen&nbsp;
Gaming for an interview about "Call of Duty:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.680
Modern Warfare II" in support of the charities&nbsp;
Game on Cancer and Call of Duty Endowment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.920
While he's proud of his Scottish heritage -- his&nbsp;
Instagram bio sports the Scottish Gaelic phrase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.920
for "Scotland forever" -- it appears that his&nbsp;
natural Scottish accent wasn't quite Scottish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:34.440
enough for Soap, so he ramped it up to make the&nbsp;
character's Glasgow origins more believable.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:38.760
"Like any accent from any country, some&nbsp;
accents are going to be thicker than others."

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:42.920
Ellice's Scottish accent is entirely absent&nbsp;
on "Loki," though. The best description of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:46.400
Hunter D-90's voice is "angry American monotone."

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.880
"Looks like your favorite&nbsp;
Loki betrayed you, Mobius."

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:52.400
Most of the time, he doesn't speak at&nbsp;
all. He just stares in moody silence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.200
Even getting to the point where he&nbsp;
could half apologize to Mobius must&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.240
have exerted every ounce of his willpower.&nbsp;
But hey, that's growth. Maybe he'll get more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:02.440
time in "Loki" Season 2 to squeeze&nbsp;
out the other half of that apology.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.640
Marvel's "Loki" Season 2 is streaming now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.667
with new episodes hitting Disney+ every&nbsp;
Thursday through November 9, 2023.

